  "serverOwnedQueryKeys": {
    "$comment": "Executor parameters only the server's credential resolver may set. A key in keys, matched exactly and case-sensitively, is refused (error) in the query of a top-level step (field stepFieldFormat) and of a loop sub-step (field loopStepFieldFormat, whose second placeholder is the sub-step's id as written). No other surface is scanned. A new server-owned key is a change to keys. Reference: validateNoServerOwnedStepQueryKeys, IsServerOwnedParamKey (CFX-05, after v2.790.0).",
    "keys": [
      "aiv_api_key",
      "aiv_base_url",
      "aiv_delegation"
    ],
    "stepFieldFormat": "steps.%s.query.%s",
    "loopStepFieldFormat": "steps.%s.loop.steps.%s.query.%s"
  },
  "credentialEndpointPairing": {
    "$comment": "credential_endpoint_unpaired (WARNING, never an error): the one statically certain shape of AIgentFlow's run-time credential/endpoint pairing refusal. ai: an ai://<provider>/... step (top-level or loop sub-step) whose query holds a non-empty string <provider>+providerBaseUrlParamSuffix while neither its query (genericKeyParam or <provider>+providerKeyParamSuffix, non-empty strings) nor executor_config.<provider>.api_key (a literal, not an env reference) supplies a key; and executor_config.<provider>.base_url for a provider in executorConfigProviders when it is a literal, the block has no literal api_key, and it is not the case that at least one step uses the provider and every such step brings its own query key. keylessProviders are exempt from both. families: a step whose executor resolves (protocolAliases first, then the key protocol+familyKeySeparator+driver, else protocol) to a row. implicitServerCredential rows are never judged. A row with storedKeyShape warns on the first non-empty string endpointParam in the query unless the query holds an own key (a non-empty string in ownKeyParams, or a mapping under ownCredentialsMapParam). Any other row warns when its secret (the first non-empty string secretParam in the query, else per configKey in order: executor_config api_key when configApiKeyParam is a secretParam, else the first non-empty string secretParam under extra) is exactly an env reference to a serverEnv name on a row with expandsServerEnvReferences, and its endpoint (the first non-empty string endpointParam in the query, else per configKey: base_url when configBaseUrlParam is an endpointParam, else the first non-empty string endpointParam under extra) is a literal: no templateActionOpen, not an env reference, and not of the same origin as a defaultEndpoint (lower-cased scheme://host:port, defaultPorts filled). serverEnv is the reference's per-family server-variable set, evaluated. Field formats are the reference's. Reference: validateCredentialEndpointPairing (DC-FORGE-231) and validateFamilyCredentialEndpointPairing (DC-FORGE-233).",
    "stepFieldFormat": "steps.%s.query.%s",
    "loopStepFieldFormat": "steps.%s.loop.steps.%s.query.%s",
    "executorConfigBaseUrlFieldFormat": "executor_config.%s.base_url",
    "executorConfigKeyFieldFormat": "executor_config.%s.%s",
    "executorConfigExtraFieldFormat": "executor_config.%s.extra.%s",
    "executorConfigApiKeyField": "api_key",
    "executorConfigBaseUrlField": "base_url",
    "protocolSeparator": "://",
    "defaultPorts": {
      "http": "80",
      "https": "443"
    },
    "ai": {
      "protocol": "ai",
      "genericKeyParam": "api_key",
      "providerKeyParamSuffix": "_api_key",
      "providerBaseUrlParamSuffix": "_base_url",
      "keylessProviders": [
